window.ADVENT={"title":"Advent","season":2026,"start":"2026-11-29","translation":"BSB","days":[{"d":1,"w":"Hope","t":"Light in the dark","r":"Isaiah 9:2","x":"The people walking in darkness have seen a great light; on those living in the land of the shadow of death, a light has dawned.","teach":["Advent begins in the dark on purpose. Isaiah spoke to people who had watched their land overrun and their hope go quiet. He didn't tell them the dark wasn't real. He told them a light was coming that the dark could not stop.","Maybe this season finds you in the land of the shadow: grief, a hard diagnosis, a marriage under strain, a bank balance that keeps you up at night. Advent doesn't ask you to pretend. It asks you to wait with your eyes open, the way you watch the sky before sunrise.","For the next 27 days you'll walk toward Christmas one reading at a time: hope, then peace, then joy, then love. Start tonight with one small act of waiting on purpose."],"pray":"Lord, You see the dark places in my life that I don't talk about. I'm waiting for Your light. Teach me to wait with hope instead of dread, and let this season bring me closer to You. Amen.","do":"If you have a candle, light it tonight and sit with it for five minutes, phone in another room. Name one dark place you want God's light to reach."},{"d":2,"w":"Hope","t":"The first promise","r":"Genesis 3:15","x":"And I will put enmity between you and the woman, and between your seed and her seed. He will crush your head, and you will strike his heel.”","teach":["The first promise of Christmas was spoken in a garden, right after everything went wrong. Adam and Eve had believed the serpent's lie, and before God sent them out of Eden, He made a promise: a child of the woman would one day crush the serpent's head.","Notice the cost inside the promise. The serpent would strike his heel. Christians have read this verse for centuries as the first whisper of the gospel: a Savior who would win, and be wounded winning.","God's answer to the worst day in human history was a promise about a child. Whatever went wrong in your story, His plan to rescue you is older than your mistake."],"pray":"Father, thank You that Your rescue started the moment we fell. I bring You the places where I have believed lies about You and about myself. Crush what is crushing me, and help me trust the Savior You promised. Amen.","do":"Write down one lie you have believed this year, then write the truth beside it. Keep the paper where you'll see it this week."},{"d":3,"w":"Hope","t":"A shoot from a stump","r":"Isaiah 11:1-2","x":"Then a shoot will spring up from the stump of Jesse, and a Branch from his roots will bear fruit. The Spirit of the LORD will rest on Him—the Spirit of wisdom and understanding, the Spirit of counsel and strength, the Spirit of knowledge and fear of the LORD.","teach":["Jesse was King David's father. Isaiah could see the ax coming for David's royal line, and within a few generations the family tree looked like a stump. Nobody expects new life from a stump.","But God promised a shoot would spring up from it, a Branch, and the Spirit of the LORD would rest on Him. Seven centuries later, a baby from David's family was born in David's town.","Look at the stumps in your own life: the career that ended, the friendship that died, the dream you buried. God brings growth out of what looks finished. Hope isn't denial. It's watching a stump for green."],"pray":"Lord, there are things in my life that look cut down and finished. I give them to You. Grow what You want to grow, and give me eyes to see the first green shoot. Amen.","do":"Text one person you've lost touch with. Not to fix everything, just to say you thought of them."},{"d":4,"w":"Hope","t":"Like a watchman","r":"Psalm 130:5-6","x":"I wait for the LORD; my soul does wait, and in His word I put my hope. My soul waits for the Lord more than watchmen wait for the morning—more than watchmen wait for the morning.","teach":["A night watchman's job is simple and hard: stay awake, stay at your post, and wait for the sun. He can't make morning come faster. He can only be ready when it does.","The psalmist says his soul waits for the Lord more than that, and he says it twice. This isn't passive waiting. His hope is planted in God's word, because God's word is the one thing in the night that doesn't move.","Most of us hate waiting, so we fill it with noise. Today, wait like a watchman: quiet, alert, with your eyes on the horizon where God has promised to show up."],"pray":"Lord, I'm waiting on You for things I can't fix myself. Keep me at my post. Put my hope in Your word, not in my timeline, and let me see the morning when it comes. Amen.","do":"Spend ten minutes today in silence: no music, no scrolling. When your mind wanders, pray one line: I wait for You, Lord."},{"d":5,"w":"Hope","t":"Strength for the wait","r":"Isaiah 40:31","x":"But those who wait upon the LORD will renew their strength; they will mount up with wings like eagles; they will run and not grow weary, they will walk and not faint.","teach":["Isaiah 40 was written to tired people. God's people had waited so long for Him to act that they had started saying their way was hidden from Him.","God's answer wasn't a schedule. It was strength: “those who wait upon the LORD will renew their strength”. Some days that looks like soaring. Some days it looks like walking and not fainting, and that counts too.","December can drain you: deadlines, family pressure, more spending than you planned. You don't have to soar this week. Ask God for the strength to take the next step faithfully."],"pray":"Lord, I'm tired, and the season is just getting started. Renew my strength. When I can't run, help me walk, and when I can't walk, carry me. Amen.","do":"Pick one thing on your December list you can drop or hand off this week, and do it today."},{"d":6,"w":"Hope","t":"The days are coming","r":"Jeremiah 33:14-15","x":"Behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when I will fulfill the gracious promise that I have spoken to the house of Israel and the house of Judah. In those days and at that time I will cause to sprout for David a righteous Branch, and He will administer justice and righteousness in the land.","teach":["Jeremiah spoke these words while Babylon's army surrounded Jerusalem and he himself was confined for preaching. It was the worst possible moment to promise a righteous King from David's line. That is exactly when God told him to.","God calls it a “gracious promise” and says He will fulfill it. The promise never depended on how things looked in Jerusalem. It depended on who God is.","Your circumstances this week are not the final word on your life. Hold on to what God has said, and say it out loud when the news, the bills or the doctor's report try to have the last word."],"pray":"Faithful God, You keep Your promises even when everything around me says You won't. I trust who You are more than what I see. Help me hold on until I see what You've promised. Amen.","do":"Write one of God's promises on a card or a sticky note and put it where you'll see it every morning."},{"d":7,"w":"Hope","t":"The God of hope","r":"Romans 15:13","x":"Now may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace as you believe in Him, so that you may overflow with hope by the power of the Holy Spirit.","teach":["Paul calls Him the God of hope. Hope isn't something you manufacture by thinking positive. It's something God fills you with as you trust Him.","Notice the order. Joy and peace come as you believe, and then you overflow with hope by the power of the Holy Spirit. Overflow means it spills onto the people around you. Your hope is meant to be noticed.","This ends the first week of Advent. Ask God who in your life is running low on hope, and let some of yours spill onto them."],"pray":"God of hope, fill me with joy and peace as I trust You. Let it overflow onto my family, my coworkers and the people who are struggling this season. Amen.","do":"Encourage one person who's going through a hard season. A call, a note or a meal is better than a like."},{"d":8,"w":"Peace","t":"Prince of Peace","r":"Isaiah 9:6","x":"For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given, and the government will be upon His shoulders. And He will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.","teach":["This week's theme is peace. If you're lighting candles, light the second one today. Isaiah gives the promised child four names, and the last is Prince of Peace.","The peace He brings is bigger than a calm afternoon. The Hebrew word is shalom: wholeness, things put right between you and God, you and other people, and you and yourself. A prince doesn't just feel peaceful. He rules, and His rule makes peace real.","Where is your life most unsettled right now? Before you try to fix it, invite the Prince of Peace to rule there. Peace starts with who's in charge."],"pray":"Jesus, Prince of Peace, I want Your rule in the places I've been running myself. Bring wholeness where there's been worry, conflict and hurry. Amen.","do":"Name the one area where you feel least at peace, and pray about it before you talk to anyone else about it today."},{"d":9,"w":"Peace","t":"Speak tenderly","r":"Isaiah 40:1-2","x":"“Comfort, comfort My people,” says your God. “Speak tenderly to Jerusalem, and proclaim to her that her forced labor has been completed; her iniquity has been pardoned. For she has received from the hand of the LORD double for all her sins.”","teach":["After thirty-nine chapters of hard words, Isaiah turns a corner, and the first thing God says is comfort, twice. He tells His messengers to speak tenderly.","God announces that the hard season is over and His people's iniquity is pardoned. Christians hear that announcement fulfilled in Jesus: your debt isn't just reduced. It's paid.","Many of us talk to ourselves harshly, in a voice God never uses with His children. Today, speak to yourself the way God speaks to you: tenderly, truthfully, with your pardon already settled."],"pray":"Father, thank You for speaking comfort over me. Quiet the harsh voice in my head with Your tender one. I receive the pardon You paid for. Amen.","do":"Notice one harsh thing you say to yourself today. Write it down, cross it out, and write what God says about you instead."},{"d":10,"w":"Peace","t":"What should we do?","r":"Luke 3:10-11","x":"The crowds asked him, “What then should we do?” John replied, “Whoever has two tunics should share with him who has none, and whoever has food should do the same.”","teach":["John the Baptist prepared people for Jesus with a hard message about turning back to God, and the crowds asked him a simple question: “What then should we do?” His answer was practical. Share your extra coat. Share your food.","Peace with God changes how we hold our stuff. Repentance isn't only feeling sorry. It's turning around, and often you can see the turn in your closet and your pantry.","December is the season of more. Let it also be the season of sharing. Look at what you have two of, and ask who has none."],"pray":"Lord, I want my life to show that I belong to You. Loosen my grip on what I have, and show me who needs what I can share this week. Amen.","do":"Give away one coat, blanket or bag of groceries this week to a shelter, a food pantry or a neighbor who needs it."},{"d":11,"w":"Peace","t":"Peace with God","r":"Romans 5:1","x":"Therefore, since we have been justified through faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ,","teach":["Before you can feel the peace of God, you need peace with God. Paul says it comes one way: justified through faith, through our Lord Jesus Christ.","Justified is a courtroom word. It means declared right. You don't earn it by having a good year. Jesus earned it for you, and faith receives it.","Many people spend December trying to feel at peace while quietly believing God is disappointed in them. If you trust Christ, the war is over. Live today as someone God is at peace with."],"pray":"Jesus, thank You for making peace between me and God. I stop trying to earn what You already gave. Let me rest in being declared right by You. Amen.","do":"Read Romans 5:1-11 slowly today and underline every phrase that describes what God has already done."},{"d":12,"w":"Peace","t":"Not as the world gives","r":"John 14:27","x":"Peace I leave with you; My peace I give to you. I do not give to you as the world gives. Do not let your hearts be troubled; do not be afraid.","teach":["Jesus said these words the night before He died, to friends who were about to watch everything fall apart. He didn't promise them an easy week. He gave them His peace.","The world's peace depends on circumstances: when the bills are paid, when the test comes back clear, when the family gets along. Jesus' peace holds when none of that is true, because it rests on Him.","He follows the gift with two commands: don't let your hearts be troubled, and don't be afraid. That means you have a part to play. You can choose what your heart dwells on."],"pray":"Jesus, I receive Your peace, the kind the world can't give or take away. When my heart starts to spiral, turn it back to You. Amen.","do":"Every time you catch yourself worrying today, stop and pray one sentence: Jesus, I take Your peace."},{"d":13,"w":"Peace","t":"Guarded","r":"Philippians 4:6-7","x":"Be anxious for nothing, but in everything, by prayer and petition, with thanksgiving, present your requests to God. And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your minds in Christ Jesus.","teach":["Paul wrote this letter as a prisoner. He knew anxiety. His instruction isn't to stuff it down but to turn it into prayer: everything, with thanksgiving.","Then comes the promise. The peace of God will guard your heart and your mind. Guard is a soldier's word, a sentry posted at the gate. You don't have to stand watch over your worries all night. God posts His peace there.","Thanksgiving is the part we skip. It's hard to stay anxious and grateful at the same time. Try it today: bring every worry to God with one thing you're thankful for."],"pray":"Father, here is what's worrying me today. I bring it to You with thanks for all You've already done. Guard my heart and my mind with Your peace. Amen.","do":"Write down three worries. Next to each one, write something you're thankful for, then pray through the list."},{"d":14,"w":"Peace","t":"Swords into plowshares","r":"Isaiah 2:4","x":"Then He will judge between the nations and arbitrate for many peoples. They will beat their swords into plowshares and their spears into pruning hooks. Nation will no longer take up the sword against nation, nor train anymore for war.","teach":["Isaiah saw a day when nations would beat their weapons into farm tools. Swords into plowshares means taking what was made to hurt and turning it into something that feeds people.","That day isn't fully here yet. But Advent people live toward it now. The peace Jesus brings is meant to reach the conflicts in our own homes, churches and workplaces.","Is there a relationship where you've kept your sword sharp? Today, take one step toward peace: an apology, a softer answer, or the conversation you've been avoiding."],"pray":"Lord, make me a peacemaker. Show me where I've been armed for a fight, and give me the courage to turn it into something that heals. Amen.","do":"Take one step toward peace with someone today: apologize, forgive, or reach out first."},{"d":15,"w":"Joy","t":"The Lord is near","r":"Philippians 4:4-5","x":"Rejoice in the Lord always. I will say it again: Rejoice! Let your gentleness be apparent to all. The Lord is near.","teach":["The third week of Advent is about joy. If you're lighting candles, light the third one. Paul says to rejoice in the Lord always, and then he says it again, as if he knew we'd need to hear it twice.","Joy in the Lord is different from happiness about your circumstances. Paul wasn't writing from a comfortable place. His joy came from the last line: “The Lord is near.”","Near in time, and near in presence. Jesus came near at Christmas, He is near by His Spirit now, and He is coming again. Whatever this week holds, you don't face it alone."],"pray":"Lord, You are near. Teach me to rejoice in You even when my circumstances are hard, and let my gentleness be obvious to everyone this week. Amen.","do":"Before bed, write down five gifts from God you noticed today, small or big."},{"d":16,"w":"Joy","t":"Sorrow will flee","r":"Isaiah 35:10","x":"So the redeemed of the LORD will return and enter Zion with singing, crowned with everlasting joy. Gladness and joy will overtake them, and sorrow and sighing will flee.","teach":["Isaiah paints the end of the story: God's people walking home with singing, crowned with everlasting joy. Sorrow and sighing don't just shrink. They flee.","Christian joy isn't pretending there's no sorrow. It's knowing how the story ends. Grief is real, and the holidays can make it louder. But sorrow doesn't get the last word.","If this season is hard because someone is missing, let today be honest. Tell God about your sorrow, then read this verse again as a promise about where your story is headed."],"pray":"Lord, You know what makes this season heavy for me. I bring You my sorrow. Hold me in it, and fix my eyes on the day when sorrow and sighing flee. Amen.","do":"Reach out to someone who's grieving this Christmas. Say their loved one's name. It matters more than you think."},{"d":17,"w":"Joy","t":"Let it be","r":"Luke 1:38","x":"“I am the Lord’s servant,” Mary answered. “May it happen to me according to your word.” Then the angel left her.","teach":["The angel had just told Mary, a young woman from an overlooked town, that she would carry the Son of God. Her plans, her reputation and her engagement were suddenly all in question.","Her answer is one of the bravest sentences in Scripture. “I am the Lord’s servant,” she said, and she asked for it to happen just as God had said. She didn't have the whole plan. She had the One who did.","Joy often starts with surrender. What has God been asking you to say yes to? There's joy on the other side of the yes you keep putting off."],"pray":"Lord, I am Your servant. I don't see the whole plan, but I trust You. Let Your word happen in my life, in Your way and in Your time. Amen.","do":"Tell God yes about one thing you've been resisting. Then tell one person, so you follow through."},{"d":18,"w":"Joy","t":"The baby leaped","r":"Luke 1:41","x":"When Elizabeth heard Mary’s greeting, the baby leaped in her womb, and Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit.","teach":["Mary, newly pregnant, travels to see her relative Elizabeth, who is six months along with the boy who will become John the Baptist. The moment Elizabeth hears Mary's greeting, the baby leaps in her womb.","Before Jesus spoke a word or worked a miracle, His presence brought joy into the room. An unborn prophet recognized his King.","Joy is contagious when Jesus is in the room, and if you belong to Him, you carry Him into every room you enter. Who could you visit this week?"],"pray":"Jesus, fill me with Your Spirit the way You filled Elizabeth. Let Your presence in me bring joy into every room I walk into this week. Amen.","do":"Visit or call an older relative or friend this week, and tell them they matter to you."},{"d":19,"w":"Joy","t":"My soul magnifies the Lord","r":"Luke 1:46-48","x":"Then Mary said: “My soul magnifies the Lord, and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior! For He has looked with favor on the humble state of His servant. From now on all generations will call me blessed.","teach":["Mary's song is called the Magnificat, from its first word in Latin. To magnify something is to make it look as big as it really is. Mary made God big and her worries small.","Notice what she celebrates: He looked with favor on the humble. God didn't choose a palace. He chose a young woman nobody important had heard of, and she knew it.","Your praise doesn't need perfect circumstances. It needs a true-sized view of God. Today, magnify Him by saying out loud what He has done for you."],"pray":"My soul magnifies You, Lord. You are bigger than every problem I've been staring at. Thank You for looking with favor on someone as ordinary as me. Amen.","do":"Make a short list titled Great things God has done for me, and read it out loud tonight."},{"d":20,"w":"Joy","t":"He sings over you","r":"Zephaniah 3:17","x":"The LORD your God is among you; He is mighty to save. He will rejoice over you with gladness; He will quiet you with His love; He will rejoice over you with singing.”","teach":["Zephaniah spends most of his short book warning about judgment. Then, near the end, comes this: God will rejoice over His people with singing.","Many of us picture God putting up with us at best. Zephaniah pictures Him delighting in His people, quieting them with His love the way a parent hums over a child who can't sleep.","Advent joy isn't only our joy in God. It's God's joy over us. Let that land today: if you are His, He is glad you're His."],"pray":"Father, it's hard for me to believe You rejoice over me. Quiet me with Your love today, and let me hear Your song over my life. Amen.","do":"Play one worship song today and listen to the words without doing anything else."},{"d":21,"w":"Joy","t":"Sown in tears","r":"Psalm 126:5-6","x":"Those who sow in tears will reap with shouts of joy. He who goes out weeping, bearing a trail of seed, will surely return with shouts of joy, carrying sheaves of grain.","teach":["This psalm was sung by people God had brought home from captivity to a ruined land. They had to plant crops in hard ground, with tears in their eyes.","God's promise is that tears planted in faith come back as a harvest of joy. The weeping is real, and so is the harvest.","What are you sowing in tears right now? A prodigal child, a hard marriage, a business that's struggling? Keep sowing. Joy is coming with the sheaves."],"pray":"Lord, I've been sowing in tears. I trust You with the harvest. Keep me faithful in the planting, and let me see joy come back in Your time. Amen.","do":"Do the next faithful thing in the hard situation you're praying about, even if it's small."},{"d":22,"w":"Love","t":"So loved","r":"John 3:16","x":"For God so loved the world that He gave His one and only Son, that everyone who believes in Him shall not perish but have eternal life.","teach":["The fourth week of Advent is about love. If you're lighting candles, light the fourth one. This is the most famous verse in the Bible, and it's famous because it says everything in one breath.","God so loved the world that He gave. Love that only feels isn't the love of Christmas. God's love gave His one and only Son, and He gave Him for people who weren't loving Him back.","This week, let your love do something. Give where it costs you, to someone who can't repay you."],"pray":"Father, thank You for loving me enough to give Your Son. Make my love more than words this week, and show me who to give to. Amen.","do":"Do something generous for someone who can't pay you back, and don't post about it."},{"d":23,"w":"Love","t":"The longest night","r":"John 1:4-5","x":"In Him was life, and that life was the light of men. The Light shines in the darkness, and the darkness has not overcome it.","teach":["Tonight is the longest night of the year in the Northern Hemisphere. From here on, the days get longer. John's Gospel puts it this way: “The Light shines in the darkness, and the darkness has not overcome it.”","Christmas didn't end all the darkness in the world. It did something better. It brought a Light the darkness can't put out, and that Light is a person.","For many people this is the hardest week of the year. If that's you, you're not weak and you're not alone. The night is long, but it isn't winning. If you're in crisis, call or text 988 in the US."],"pray":"Jesus, Light of the world, shine into the darkest corner of my life tonight. When the night feels long, remind me that the darkness has not overcome You. Amen.","do":"Tonight, turn off every light for one minute, then light one candle or lamp, and thank God His Light is still shining."},{"d":24,"w":"Love","t":"Small among the clans","r":"Micah 5:2","x":"But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, who are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come forth for Me One to be ruler over Israel—One whose origins are of old, from the days of eternity.","teach":["About seven hundred years before Jesus, Micah named the town where the King would be born. Not Jerusalem, the capital. Bethlehem, “small among the clans of Judah”.","God keeps choosing small: a small town, a young couple, a feeding trough. The One whose origins are from the days of eternity chose to arrive somewhere easy to overlook.","You may feel small this season: small income, small church, small influence. God isn't looking past you. Small places are where He loves to show up."],"pray":"Lord, thank You for choosing small places. When I feel overlooked, remind me that You were born in a town most people passed by. Use my small life for Your big love. Amen.","do":"Thank someone whose work usually goes unnoticed: a custodian, a cashier, a nursery volunteer."},{"d":25,"w":"Love","t":"God with us","r":"Matthew 1:23","x":"“Behold, the virgin will be with child and will give birth to a son, and they will call Him Immanuel” (which means, “God with us”).","teach":["Matthew quotes Isaiah and then translates the name for us: Immanuel means “God with us”. Not God near us, or God watching from a distance. God with us.","Joseph is part of this story too. He had planned to end his engagement quietly, but after the angel spoke, he took Mary as his wife and named the child Jesus. Love obeyed before it fully understood.","Christmas means God came to live among us. Wherever you are tomorrow, the kitchen, the hospital, the long drive or the empty apartment, God is with you there."],"pray":"Immanuel, thank You for being God with us. Be with me in every room I walk into this Christmas, and help me be present with the people You've given me. Amen.","do":"Put your phone away during one meal tomorrow and be fully with the people at the table."},{"d":26,"w":"Love","t":"No room","r":"Luke 2:6-7","x":"While they were there, the time came for her Child to be born. And she gave birth to her firstborn, a Son. She wrapped Him in swaddling cloths and laid Him in a manger, because there was no room for them in the inn.","teach":["The Son of God was born where animals were fed and laid in a manger, because there was no room for them in the inn. The King of the universe began His life on earth crowded out.","Christmas Eve is busy for most of us: last gifts, cooking, travel, family. It's easy for Jesus to get crowded out of His own birthday.","Tonight, make room. It doesn't have to be fancy. Read the Christmas story out loud, with whoever is with you or by yourself, and give Him the best seat in the house."],"pray":"Jesus, I'm sorry for the times I've crowded You out. Tonight I make room for You. Be the center of my Christmas and of my life. Amen.","do":"Read Luke 2:1-20 out loud tonight, with family or friends if you can."},{"d":27,"w":"Christmas","t":"Good news of great joy","r":"Luke 2:10-12","x":"But the angel said to them, “Do not be afraid! For behold, I bring you good news of great joy that will be for all the people: Today in the city of David a Savior has been born to you. He is Christ the Lord! And this will be a sign to you: You will find a baby wrapped in swaddling cloths and lying in a manger.”","teach":["Merry Christmas. The first people to hear the news were shepherds working the night shift, far from the center of anything. The angel's first words were: “Do not be afraid!”","The news is “good news of great joy that will be for all the people” and it is this: a Savior has been born. Not only a teacher, not only an example, but a Savior, Christ the Lord, wrapped in cloths and lying in a manger.","Advent was the waiting. Today is the arrival. Whatever this day looks like for you, the news is the same: He came for you."],"pray":"Jesus, welcome. Thank You for coming for me. Let the joy of this day last longer than the wrapping paper, and help me share this good news with someone who needs it. Amen.","do":"Tell one person today, in your own words, why Jesus' birth matters to you."}]};window.LENT={"title":"Lent","season":2027,"start":"2027-02-10","translation":"BSB","days":[{"d":1,"w":"Return","t":"Ash Wednesday: come back","r":"Joel 2:12-13","x":"“Yet even now,” declares the LORD, “return to Me with all your heart, with fasting, weeping, and mourning.” So rend your hearts and not your garments, and return to the LORD your God. For He is gracious and compassionate, slow to anger, abounding in loving devotion. And He relents from sending disaster.","teach":["Lent starts with an invitation, not a scolding. Through Joel, God says “return to Me with all your heart”, and then tells you why it's safe to come back: He is gracious, compassionate and slow to anger.","For the next 47 days, Ash Wednesday to Easter, you'll practice the three old disciplines of Lent: pray, fast and give. They line up with the three pillars of Flourish. Prayer rebuilds your relationships, with God first. Fasting retrains your body and appetites. Giving loosens money's grip on your heart.","Joel says to tear your heart, not your clothes. Lent isn't a show of being sorry. It's turning around, on the inside first."],"pray":"Lord, I'm coming back. I've drifted in ways I know and ways I don't. Thank You for being gracious and slow to anger. Use these weeks to turn my whole heart toward You again. Amen.","do":"Choose one thing to pray, one thing to fast from and one thing to give during Lent. Write all three down where you'll see them."},{"d":2,"w":"Return","t":"A clean heart","r":"Psalm 51:10-12","x":"Create in me a clean heart, O God, and renew a right spirit within me. Cast me not away from Your presence; take not Your Holy Spirit from me. Restore to me the joy of Your salvation, and sustain me with a willing spirit.","teach":["David wrote this psalm after the worst season of his life: adultery, a cover-up and a man dead because of him. He doesn't ask God to tidy up his reputation. He asks for a new heart.","Notice what he wants back: the joy of God's salvation. Sin doesn't only make us guilty. It makes us joyless, tired, hiding. Repentance is the road back to joy, not away from it.","You don't have to fix yourself before you pray this. Create means God makes what wasn't there. Bring Him the heart you have, and ask for the one you need."],"pray":"Create in me a clean heart, O God. You know what I've done and what I've hidden. Renew a right spirit in me, and give me back the joy I've lost. Amen.","do":"Read all of Psalm 51 slowly today. Underline one line and pray it every time you pick up your phone."},{"d":3,"w":"Return","t":"The fast God chose","r":"Isaiah 58:6-7","x":"Isn’t this the fast that I have chosen: to break the chains of wickedness, to untie the cords of the yoke, to set the oppressed free and tear off every yoke? Isn’t it to share your bread with the hungry, to bring the poor and homeless into your home, to clothe the naked when you see him, and not to turn away from your own flesh and blood?","teach":["God's people in Isaiah's day were fasting and wondering why God didn't seem impressed. His answer stung. They skipped meals while ignoring the hungry and the poor.","Through Isaiah, God describes “the fast that I have chosen”: breaking chains, freeing the oppressed, sharing bread, opening your home. A fast that leaves your neighbor hungry has missed the point.","As you plan your Lent, let your fast and your giving work together. What you stop spending on yourself can feed someone else."],"pray":"Lord, I don't want a fast that only looks holy. Open my eyes to the hungry and the hurting around me, and make my sacrifice someone else's relief. Amen.","do":"Pick a cause for your Lenten giving today: a food pantry, a shelter or a family you know. Every time you skip something, set that money aside for it."},{"d":4,"w":"Return","t":"While he was still far away","r":"Luke 15:20","x":"So he got up and went to his father. But while he was still in the distance, his father saw him and was filled with compassion. He ran to his son, embraced him, and kissed him.","teach":["The younger son had wasted his share of his father's estate. He came home rehearsing a speech about working as a hired hand. He never got to give it the way he planned.","While he was still in the distance, his father saw him. That means the father had been watching the road. He ran, which a respected man in that culture would not do, and embraced his son before a single word of apology.","That is the Father you're returning to this Lent. You don't earn the welcome by the speech. The welcome is already running toward you."],"pray":"Father, I've been far away in ways that matter. Thank You for watching the road for me. I'm coming home. Help me believe I'm welcome. Amen.","do":"Is there someone waiting for you to come home, to a call, an apology or a visit? Take one step toward them this week."},{"d":5,"w":"Wilderness","t":"Led into the wilderness","r":"Matthew 4:1-2","x":"Then Jesus was led by the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil. After fasting forty days and forty nights, He was hungry.","teach":["This first week of Lent follows Jesus into the desert. Right after His baptism, the Spirit led Him there, and He fasted forty days and forty nights. Lent's forty days come from this.","The wilderness wasn't punishment. The Spirit led Him there. Sometimes God leads you into a dry, hungry season on purpose, not because He's angry but because that's where trust gets real.","If you're in a wilderness season right now, you're not off the map. The same Spirit who led Jesus in also carried Him through."],"pray":"Spirit of God, if You've led me into a dry season, teach me what You want me to learn here. Keep me close when I'm hungry and tired. Amen.","do":"Name your wilderness, the hard place you're in right now, and write one sentence about what you think God might be teaching you there."},{"d":6,"w":"Wilderness","t":"Not by bread alone","r":"Matthew 4:3-4","x":"The tempter came to Him and said, “If You are the Son of God, tell these stones to become bread.” But Jesus answered, “It is written: ‘Man shall not live on bread alone, but on every word that comes from the mouth of God.’”","teach":["The first temptation came when Jesus was at His hungriest. Turn the stones into bread. It wasn't wrong to eat. It was wrong to use His power to serve Himself outside His Father's will.","Jesus answers with Scripture: “Man shall not live on bread alone”. Our appetites, for food, comfort, approval and money, are real, but they aren't the deepest thing in us.","When an appetite starts making your decisions, answer it the way Jesus did, with God's word. Have a verse ready before the temptation shows up."],"pray":"Jesus, You know what it's like to be hungry and tempted. When my appetites start running me, feed me with Your word. Amen.","do":"Memorize Matthew 4:4 today. Say it the next time a craving shows up."},{"d":7,"w":"Wilderness","t":"Don't test God","r":"Matthew 4:5-7","x":"Then the devil took Him to the holy city and set Him on the pinnacle of the temple. “If You are the Son of God,” he said, “throw Yourself down. For it is written: ‘He will command His angels concerning You, and they will lift You up in their hands, so that You will not strike Your foot against a stone.’” Jesus replied, “It is also written: ‘Do not put the Lord your God to the test.’”","teach":["The second temptation was clever. The devil quoted Scripture: jump, and the angels will catch You. It sounds like faith, but it's really an attempt to force God's hand.","Jesus refused. Trusting God means following Him, not daring Him to prove Himself on your terms. Plenty of reckless choices get dressed up as faith.","Where are you tempted to make a risky decision and call it trusting God? Faith walks with God. It doesn't jump ahead and demand He catch you."],"pray":"Lord, I don't want to test You. I want to trust You. Show me where I've confused my own wants with faith, and give me patience to follow Your lead. Amen.","do":"Before any big decision this week, ask two people you trust for their honest opinion, and listen."},{"d":8,"w":"Wilderness","t":"Worship Him only","r":"Matthew 4:8-10","x":"Again, the devil took Him to a very high mountain and showed Him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory. “All this I will give You,” he said, “if You will fall down and worship me.” “Away from Me, Satan!” Jesus told him. “For it is written: ‘Worship the Lord your God and serve Him only.’”","teach":["The last temptation was the biggest offer: every kingdom in the world, for one act of worship. A shortcut to everything, without the cross.","Jesus sent the devil away and quoted Scripture again: worship God and serve Him only. Everything has an asking price. What you bow to eventually owns you.","Shortcuts still tempt us: cut the corner at work, fudge the numbers, compromise just this once to get ahead. The kingdom Jesus gained came the long way, through obedience."],"pray":"Lord, You alone are worth my worship. Expose the shortcuts I'm tempted to take, and give me the courage to do the right thing the long way. Amen.","do":"Identify one shortcut you've been tempted to take, at work, with money or in a relationship, and decide today to take the long, honest way."},{"d":9,"w":"Wilderness","t":"Manna in the desert","r":"Deuteronomy 8:3","x":"He humbled you, and in your hunger He gave you manna to eat, which neither you nor your fathers had known, so that you might understand that man does not live on bread alone, but on every word that comes from the mouth of the LORD.","teach":["Jesus answered His first temptation with this verse. Moses spoke it to Israel after forty years of manna, bread that appeared each morning, just enough for one day.","God let them be hungry so they would learn where life really comes from. Daily bread teaches daily trust. You can't stockpile manna, and you can't stockpile faith.","What would it look like to trust God for just today: today's strength, today's provision, today's patience?"],"pray":"Father, teach me daily trust. I want to stockpile security, and You keep giving me enough for today. Thank You for today's bread. Amen.","do":"Tonight, write down three ways God provided for you today, however small."},{"d":10,"w":"Wilderness","t":"He gets it","r":"Hebrews 4:15-16","x":"For we do not have a high priest who is unable to sympathize with our weaknesses, but we have one who was tempted in every way that we are, yet was without sin. Let us then approach the throne of grace with confidence, so that we may receive mercy and find grace to help us in our time of need.","teach":["Jesus was tempted in every way that we are. Not in a theoretical way. He felt the pull, and He didn't give in.","That's why the next line is so bold: come to the throne of grace with confidence. The One on the throne isn't shocked by your struggle. He knows it from the inside, and He has mercy and help for this exact moment.","If you're fighting a habit you're ashamed of, don't hide from God until you've won. Run to Him in the middle of the fight, and tell one trusted person too. If you're in crisis, call or text 988 in the US."],"pray":"Jesus, You know what temptation feels like. I'm coming to You with confidence, not because I'm strong, but because You're merciful. Help me in my time of need. Amen.","do":"Tell one trusted friend or pastor about a struggle you've been carrying alone this Lent."},{"d":11,"w":"Wilderness","t":"A way out","r":"1 Corinthians 10:13","x":"No temptation has seized you except what is common to man. And God is faithful; He will not let you be tempted beyond what you can bear. But when you are tempted, He will also provide an escape, so that you can stand up under it.","teach":["Temptation lies to you in two ways: no one else struggles like this, and you have no choice. Paul answers both. Your temptation is common to man, and God is faithful.","God promises a way of escape. Often it's simple and unglamorous: leave the room, close the app, call a friend, go to bed. The way out usually shows up early, before the temptation is at full strength.","Plan your exits ahead of time. Decide now what you'll do the next time the pull comes."],"pray":"Faithful God, thank You that I'm not alone and not trapped. Show me the way out when temptation comes, and give me the humility to take it early. Amen.","do":"Write your escape plan for your most common temptation: when it starts, I will ___. Put it in your phone's notes."},{"d":12,"w":"Prayer","t":"The inner room","r":"Matthew 6:6","x":"But when you pray, go into your inner room, shut your door, and pray to your Father, who is unseen. And your Father, who sees what is done in secret, will reward you.","teach":["This week is about prayer. Jesus assumes His followers will pray, and He cares about where and why. Prayer performed for an audience has already received its reward.","So He says to go into your inner room and shut the door. Prayer is first a private conversation with a Father who sees in secret. You don't need the right words, only an honest heart.","Find your inner room this week. It might be a closet, a car in the driveway or a walk before sunrise. Same place, same time, every day."],"pray":"Father, I want to know You, not only talk about You. Meet me in the quiet place. Teach me to pray honestly. Amen.","do":"Choose a time and place for daily prayer this week. Start with ten minutes and keep it."},{"d":13,"w":"Prayer","t":"Your kingdom come","r":"Matthew 6:9-10","x":"So then, this is how you should pray: ‘Our Father in heaven, hallowed be Your name. Your kingdom come, Your will be done, on earth as it is in heaven.","teach":["When His disciples asked how to pray, Jesus gave them this. It opens with God, not us: His name, His kingdom, His will.","“Your will be done” is one of the most dangerous prayers you can pray. You're asking God to rearrange your plans around His, on earth, in your actual life, the way it's done in heaven.","Starting with God's priorities puts your own requests in their right size. Begin today's prayers with His name and His kingdom before anything else."],"pray":"Our Father in heaven, hallowed be Your name. Your kingdom come, Your will be done in my home, my work and my heart, as it is in heaven. Amen.","do":"Pray the Lord's Prayer slowly today, pausing after each line to say what it means for your life right now."},{"d":14,"w":"Prayer","t":"Daily bread, daily mercy","r":"Matthew 6:11-13","x":"Give us this day our daily bread. And forgive us our debts, as we also have forgiven our debtors. And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil one.’","teach":["The second half of the Lord's Prayer is about our needs: bread for today, forgiveness for what we've done, protection from what's coming.","Notice how forgiveness is joined at the hip: forgive us, as we also have forgiven. A heart that holds onto grudges struggles to receive grace.","Bring all three needs to God today. Ask for provision without shame. Confess without hiding. And name the person you need to forgive."],"pray":"Father, give me what I need for today. Forgive me for what I've done, and help me forgive those who've wronged me. Lead me away from temptation and keep me from evil. Amen.","do":"Write down the name of one person you need to forgive, and pray for their good by name."},{"d":15,"w":"Prayer","t":"Before the day started","r":"Mark 1:35","x":"Early in the morning, while it was still dark, Jesus got up and went out to a solitary place to pray.","teach":["The night before had been packed with healing and crowds. Early the next morning, while it was still dark, Jesus slipped away to pray.","If the Son of God needed time alone with His Father before the demands of the day, so do we. Many of us start with our phone instead, and the day decides our priorities before we do.","Try giving God the first minutes tomorrow, before email, before news, before social media."],"pray":"Lord, I want You first, before the noise. Help me get up and meet You before the day starts pulling at me. Amen.","do":"Tonight, charge your phone outside your bedroom. Tomorrow, pray before you look at it."},{"d":16,"w":"Prayer","t":"Be still","r":"Psalm 46:10","x":"“Be still and know that I am God; I will be exalted among the nations, I will be exalted over the earth.”","teach":["Psalm 46 is set in chaos: mountains falling into the sea, nations in uproar. In the middle of it, God says: “Be still and know that I am God”.","Stillness isn't laziness. It's trust. It's choosing to stop striving long enough to remember who is actually in charge of the world.","Most of us are never still. Even our quiet moments are full of screens. Practice stillness today, on purpose."],"pray":"God, I'm restless and running. Quiet my mind. Help me be still long enough to remember that You are God and I am not. Amen.","do":"Sit in silence for five minutes today with no music, no phone and no list. When your mind races, repeat: Be still."},{"d":17,"w":"Prayer","t":"Have mercy on me","r":"Luke 18:13","x":"But the tax collector stood at a distance, unwilling even to lift up his eyes to heaven. Instead, he beat his breast and said, ‘God, have mercy on me, a sinner!’","teach":["Jesus told of two men praying. One listed his good deeds. The other stood at a distance, beat his chest and prayed seven words: “God, have mercy on me, a sinner!”","Jesus said the second man went home right with God. Honest humility gets further with God than polished performance.","Some days the most honest prayer you can pray is this one. Pray it today, and mean it."],"pray":"God, have mercy on me, a sinner. I don't come with a list of good deeds. I come needing Your grace. Amen.","do":"Pray the tax collector's prayer, slowly, morning, noon and night today."},{"d":18,"w":"Prayer","t":"When you don't know what to say","r":"Romans 8:26","x":"In the same way, the Spirit helps us in our weakness. For we do not know how we ought to pray, but the Spirit Himself intercedes for us with groans too deep for words.","teach":["Sometimes prayer feels impossible: grief is too heavy, the situation too tangled, the words just aren't there.","Paul says you aren't alone even then. The Spirit helps us in our weakness and intercedes for us with groans too deep for words. Your sighs and tears aren't wasted. They're carried.","If you're out of words this week, show up anyway. Sit with God in silence. He knows what you mean."],"pray":"Holy Spirit, I don't always know how to pray. Take my sighs, my tears and my silence, and carry them to the Father. Amen.","do":"If words won't come today, write the names of the people and situations on your heart and simply hold the list before God."},{"d":19,"w":"Fasting","t":"When you fast","r":"Matthew 6:16-18","x":"When you fast, do not be somber like the hypocrites, for they disfigure their faces to show men they are fasting. Truly I tell you, they already have their full reward. But when you fast, anoint your head and wash your face, so that your fasting will not be obvious to men, but only to your Father, who is unseen. And your Father, who sees what is done in secret, will reward you.","teach":["This week is about fasting, the discipline of the body. Jesus says when you fast, not if, and He tells you to do it quietly, without making a show of it.","Fasting is giving up something good for a while to make room for God. Every hunger pang becomes a reminder to pray. It isn't about weight or punishment, and it never earns God's love.","Fasting from food isn't safe for everyone. If you're pregnant or nursing, have diabetes, take medication that needs food, or have ever struggled with an eating disorder, don't fast from food: fast from your phone, TV or another habit instead, and talk with your doctor."],"pray":"Father, teach me to want You more than my comforts. Let every hunger this week turn me toward You, and keep my fast quiet and honest. Amen.","do":"Choose your fast for this week: one meal a day, sweets, social media or streaming. When you feel the lack, pray."},{"d":20,"w":"Fasting","t":"A temple","r":"1 Corinthians 6:19-20","x":"Do you not know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit who is in you, whom you have received from God? You are not your own; you were bought at a price. Therefore glorify God with your body.","teach":["Paul tells the Corinthians their bodies are temples of the Holy Spirit. Your body isn't a machine you drive around. It's a place where God lives.","You were bought at a price, so glorify God with your body. That covers more than avoiding sin. It includes sleep, food, movement and rest.","Caring for your health isn't vanity when it's done for God. It's stewardship of the temple He lives in."],"pray":"Lord, my body belongs to You. Help me treat it as Your temple: with rest, good food, movement and purity. Amen.","do":"Pick one health habit to keep for the rest of Lent: a daily walk, an earlier bedtime or water instead of soda."},{"d":21,"w":"Fasting","t":"Training for a crown","r":"1 Corinthians 9:25-27","x":"Everyone who competes in the games trains with strict discipline. They do it for a crown that is perishable, but we do it for a crown that is imperishable. Therefore I do not run aimlessly; I do not fight like I am beating the air. No, I discipline my body and make it my slave, so that after I have preached to others, I myself will not be disqualified.","teach":["Paul knew the athletes of his day. They trained with strict discipline for a wreath that wilted in a week. He says followers of Jesus train for a crown that lasts forever.","Discipline isn't the enemy of grace. Grace saves you. Discipline trains you. Paul says he disciplines his body so his life matches his message.","What would it look like to bring an athlete's focus to your spiritual life this week, with a plan, consistency and a goal?"],"pray":"Lord, I want to run with purpose. Give me the discipline to train my body and my soul, not to earn Your love but because I already have it. Amen.","do":"Do a short workout today, and pray through it: one prayer per exercise or per lap."},{"d":22,"w":"Fasting","t":"Ten days","r":"Daniel 1:12-13","x":"“Please test your servants for ten days. Let us be given only vegetables to eat and water to drink. Then compare our appearances with those of the young men who are eating the royal food, and deal with your servants according to what you see.”","teach":["Daniel and his friends were exiles in Babylon, offered the king's rich food. They asked to eat vegetables and drink water for ten days instead, and to let the results speak.","Their choice was about faithfulness, not a diet. They refused to let a powerful culture shape their identity, even at the table.","Small, consistent choices shape who you become. What's one area where you need to quietly go against the flow for ten days?"],"pray":"Lord, give me Daniel's quiet courage. Help me make small, faithful choices that keep my heart Yours, even when everyone around me goes the other way. Amen.","do":"Set a ten-day challenge starting today, one small choice to keep, and mark each day off on a calendar."},{"d":23,"w":"Fasting","t":"Why spend money on what doesn't satisfy?","r":"Isaiah 55:1-2","x":"“Come, all you who are thirsty, come to the waters; and you without money, come, buy, and eat! Come, buy wine and milk without money and without cost! Why spend money on that which is not bread, and your labor on that which does not satisfy? Listen carefully to Me, and eat what is good, and your soul will delight in the richest of foods.","teach":["God's invitation through Isaiah sounds like a street market: come, buy, eat, without money. Then comes a hard question. Why spend money on what doesn't satisfy?","Many of us spend our paychecks and our attention on things that leave us emptier: scrolling, shopping, comfort food, chasing approval. God offers what actually fills, and it's free.","Notice this week where you reach for something that never quite satisfies, and pause to ask God for what you really need."],"pray":"Lord, I've spent so much on things that don't satisfy. Teach me to come to You hungry and to find the richest food in You. Amen.","do":"Track every non-essential purchase this week. At the end of the week, ask which ones actually satisfied."},{"d":24,"w":"Fasting","t":"Real food","r":"John 4:34","x":"Jesus explained, “My food is to do the will of Him who sent Me and to finish His work.","teach":["The disciples came back with lunch and found Jesus deep in conversation with a Samaritan woman. When they urged Him to eat, He said: “My food is to do the will of Him who sent Me”.","Doing God's will fed Him more than lunch could. There's a kind of satisfaction that only comes from purpose: from loving someone well, finishing the work God gave you, being where He wants you.","Where do you feel most alive? Often that's a clue to the work God has put in front of you."],"pray":"Jesus, make Your will my food. Give me the deep satisfaction of doing what You've called me to do, today. Amen.","do":"Do one thing today that you know God wants you to do and you've been putting off."},{"d":25,"w":"Fasting","t":"The bread of life","r":"John 6:35","x":"Jesus answered, “I am the bread of life. Whoever comes to Me will never hunger, and whoever believes in Me will never thirst.","teach":["The crowds had eaten miraculous bread the day before, and they came back hungry for more. Jesus offered them something better: “I am the bread of life.”","Every hunger points past itself. The hunger for food, love, meaning and security is real, and only Jesus can satisfy it all the way down.","As this fasting week ends, notice what your hunger taught you. What were you really hungry for?"],"pray":"Jesus, You are the bread of life. I bring You my hungers, the ones I understand and the ones I don't. Satisfy me with Yourself. Amen.","do":"Write down what your fast taught you this week, and decide whether to keep it, change it or end it."},{"d":26,"w":"Giving","t":"Give in secret","r":"Matthew 6:2-4","x":"So when you give to the needy, do not sound a trumpet before you, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and on the streets, to be honored by men. Truly I tell you, they already have their full reward. But when you give to the needy, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing, so that your giving may be in secret. And your Father, who sees what is done in secret, will reward you.","teach":["This week is about giving, the discipline of the wallet. Jesus assumes we'll give to the needy and warns against doing it for applause.","Don't let your left hand know what your right hand is doing. Give so quietly that even you don't keep score. The Father who sees in secret is the only audience that matters.","Secret giving breaks money's hold on your heart in a way public giving can't. Nobody's watching except God."],"pray":"Father, free me from needing credit. Teach me to give quietly, generously and gladly, for You alone. Amen.","do":"Give something today that no one will ever know about: an anonymous gift, a paid-for meal, an unsigned note with cash."},{"d":27,"w":"Giving","t":"Where your treasure is","r":"Matthew 6:19-21","x":"Do not store up for yourselves treasures on earth, where moth and rust destroy, and where thieves break in and steal. But store up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where moth and rust do not destroy, and where thieves do not break in and steal. For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.","teach":["Jesus doesn't say money is evil. He says it doesn't last. Moth, rust and thieves get it all eventually.","Then He tells you how to find your heart: follow your money. Where your treasure is, your heart follows. Your bank statement is a spiritual document.","Look honestly at where your money went last month. It shows what you love. Then decide where you want your heart to go next."],"pray":"Lord, I want my heart in Your kingdom. Show me where my treasure really is, and help me move it toward what lasts. Amen.","do":"Review last month's spending. Circle one thing to cut and redirect that money to giving or to paying down debt."},{"d":28,"w":"Giving","t":"A cheerful giver","r":"2 Corinthians 9:7","x":"Each one should give what he has decided in his heart to give, not out of regret or compulsion. For God loves a cheerful giver.","teach":["Paul doesn't set an amount. He tells each person to decide in their heart what to give, not reluctantly and not under pressure, because “God loves a cheerful giver.”","Cheerful giving comes from trust. When you believe God provides, letting go stops feeling like loss and starts feeling like freedom.","If giving makes you anxious, start small and plan it ahead of time. A decided gift is easier to give cheerfully than a guilty one."],"pray":"Lord, make me a cheerful giver. Replace my fear of not having enough with trust that You will provide. Amen.","do":"Decide on a regular gift to your church or a ministry, even a small one, and set it up today."},{"d":29,"w":"Giving","t":"First, not leftover","r":"Proverbs 3:9-10","x":"Honor the LORD with your wealth and with the firstfruits of all your crops; then your barns will be filled with plenty, and your vats will overflow with new wine.","teach":["Firstfruits meant the first and best of the harvest, given to God before anything else was used. It was an act of trust that the rest of the harvest would come.","This proverb isn't a get-rich promise. It's a statement about order. When God gets the first portion, everything else is put in its proper place.","Most of us give from what's left over, if anything is. Try giving first this month, before the bills, before the spending."],"pray":"Lord, I want You first, not last, in my finances. Help me honor You with my first and best, and trust You with the rest. Amen.","do":"Next payday, make your gift the first transaction, before anything else leaves your account."},{"d":30,"w":"Giving","t":"Everything she had","r":"Mark 12:43-44","x":"Jesus called His disciples to Him and said, “Truly I tell you, this poor widow has put more than all the others into the treasury. For they all contributed out of their surplus, but she out of her poverty has put in all she had to live on.”","teach":["Jesus sat across from the temple treasury and watched people give. Rich people put in large amounts. A poor widow put in two tiny coins.","Jesus said she gave more than all of them, because they gave from their surplus and she gave all she had to live on. God measures giving by what it costs, not by its size.","You don't need a lot to be generous. You need a heart that trusts God more than the coins in your hand."],"pray":"Lord, thank You that You see the small gifts. Give me a widow's heart: trusting, generous and unafraid. Amen.","do":"Give something today that you'll actually feel, time, money or something you value."},{"d":31,"w":"Giving","t":"Life isn't stuff","r":"Luke 12:15","x":"And He said to them, “Watch out! Guard yourselves against every form of greed, for one’s life does not consist in the abundance of his possessions.”","teach":["Someone asked Jesus to settle an inheritance dispute. Instead, He warned the whole crowd: “Watch out!” Greed is sneaky. It can live in anyone.","Your life doesn't consist in the abundance of your possessions. Jesus then told the story of a rich man who built bigger barns and died that night with all his plans.","Greed doesn't always look like luxury. Sometimes it looks like worry, never enough and always more. Ask God where it's hiding in you."],"pray":"Lord, guard my heart against greed. Remind me that my life is more than what I own, and teach me to be rich toward You. Amen.","do":"Find three things you own but don't use, and give them away this week."},{"d":32,"w":"Giving","t":"More blessed to give","r":"Acts 20:35","x":"In everything, I showed you that by this kind of hard work we must help the weak, remembering the words of the Lord Jesus Himself: ‘It is more blessed to give than to receive.’”","teach":["Paul quotes words of Jesus that aren't recorded in the Gospels: “It is more blessed to give than to receive.” He had lived it, working with his own hands to help the weak.","Giving blesses the giver. Generosity shapes your heart in ways that receiving never can: it makes you freer, more grateful and more like God, who gave His Son.","As this giving week ends, look back. Where did giving bless you this week?"],"pray":"Lord Jesus, You gave everything for me. Make generosity a lifelong habit in me, not a Lenten experiment. Amen.","do":"Decide which giving habit from this week you'll keep after Easter, and put it on your calendar."},{"d":33,"w":"Mercy","t":"Merciful like your Father","r":"Luke 6:36","x":"Be merciful, just as your Father is merciful.","teach":["This week is about mercy, the discipline of relationships. Jesus' command is short and impossible on our own: be merciful, just as your Father is merciful.","Mercy is giving people better than they deserve. It's how God has treated you, and it's meant to flow through you to everyone else.","Think of the person who tests your patience most. This week, practice treating them the way God treats you."],"pray":"Father, You've been so merciful to me. Make me merciful too, especially toward the people who are hardest for me to love. Amen.","do":"Do something kind for the person who frustrates you most, without telling them why."},{"d":34,"w":"Mercy","t":"Leave your gift at the altar","r":"Matthew 5:23-24","x":"So if you are offering your gift at the altar and there remember that your brother has something against you, leave your gift there before the altar. First go and be reconciled to your brother; then come and offer your gift.","teach":["Jesus says that if you remember someone has something against you while you're worshiping, stop. Go make it right first, then come back.","God cares about broken relationships so much that He'd rather you leave church early to reconcile than sing while ignoring it. Worship and relationships can't be separated.","Is there someone who has something against you? You can't control their response, but you can go first."],"pray":"Lord, show me the relationships I've left broken. Give me the humility to go first and make things right as far as it depends on me. Amen.","do":"Reach out today to someone you've hurt or have tension with. Say you're sorry for your part, without excuses."},{"d":35,"w":"Mercy","t":"Seventy-seven times","r":"Matthew 18:21-22","x":"Then Peter came to Jesus and asked, “Lord, how many times shall I forgive my brother who sins against me? Up to seven times?” Jesus answered, “I tell you, not just seven times, but seventy-seven times!","teach":["Peter thought he was being generous: forgive seven times? Jesus answered “seventy-seven times”, a number meaning stop counting.","Forgiveness isn't saying what happened was okay, and it isn't the same as trust, which has to be rebuilt. Forgiveness is releasing your claim to get even and handing the debt to God.","Some hurts need forgiving many times, every time the memory comes back. That's normal. Keep releasing it. And forgiveness never means staying in danger: if someone is harming you, get to safety and get help."],"pray":"Lord, I'm tired of counting. Help me release the debts I've been holding onto, again and again, as many times as it takes. Amen.","do":"Each time an old hurt comes to mind today, pray: I release this to You, Lord."},{"d":36,"w":"Mercy","t":"Kind and tenderhearted","r":"Ephesians 4:32","x":"Be kind and tenderhearted to one another, forgiving each other just as in Christ God forgave you.","teach":["Paul's instruction is so simple it's easy to skip: be kind, be tenderhearted, forgive. Then he gives the reason: just as in Christ God forgave you.","Kindness often gets lost in the people closest to us. We're polite with strangers and short with our spouse, our kids, our coworkers.","Today, give your kindness to the people who usually get your leftovers."],"pray":"Lord, soften my heart toward the people closest to me. Make me kind at home, not only in public. Amen.","do":"Speak three specific, kind words of appreciation to people in your household or workplace today."},{"d":37,"w":"Mercy","t":"Bear with one another","r":"Colossians 3:13","x":"Bear with one another and forgive any complaint you may have against someone else. Forgive as the Lord forgave you.","teach":["Bearing with one another means putting up with people's quirks and weaknesses without keeping a file on them. Every community needs it: families, churches, teams.","Paul's standard is high: forgive as the Lord forgave you. You were forgiven freely, fully and first, before you deserved it.","Who are you keeping a file on? Today, close it."],"pray":"Lord, I've kept files on people. I'm closing them. Help me bear with others the way You bear with me every day. Amen.","do":"Think of a complaint you keep bringing up with someone, and decide to stop bringing it up."},{"d":38,"w":"Mercy","t":"Justice, mercy, humility","r":"Micah 6:8","x":"He has shown you, O man, what is good. And what does the LORD require of you but to act justly, to love mercy, and to walk humbly with your God?","teach":["Micah's audience wanted to know what would please God. Sacrifices? Thousands of rams? God said it's simpler and harder: “to act justly, to love mercy, and to walk humbly with your God”.","Justice is doing right, especially by people who can't defend themselves. Mercy is loving to give people better than they deserve. Humility is walking with God, not ahead of Him.","Which of the three comes hardest to you right now? Practice that one today."],"pray":"Lord, teach me to act justly, love mercy and walk humbly with You, in my work, my home and my community. Amen.","do":"Do one act of justice today: speak up for someone, pay someone fairly, or keep a promise that costs you."},{"d":39,"w":"Mercy","t":"As far as the east is from the west","r":"Psalm 103:10-12","x":"He has not dealt with us according to our sins or repaid us according to our iniquities. For as high as the heavens are above the earth, so great is His loving devotion for those who fear Him. As far as the east is from the west, so far has He removed our transgressions from us.","teach":["David says God hasn't treated us as our sins deserve. Then he reaches for the biggest distances he can think of: as high as the heavens, as far as the east is from the west.","You can travel north until it becomes south, but east never meets west. That's how far God has removed the sins of those who trust Him. He isn't keeping a record to pull out later.","As we head into Holy Week, let this land: if you belong to Him, your sins are gone, not just hidden."],"pray":"Lord, thank You for not treating me as my sins deserve. Help me believe that what You've forgiven is truly gone. Amen.","do":"Write a sin you've already confessed on paper, then tear it up and throw it away as a reminder that it's gone."},{"d":40,"w":"Holy Week","t":"Palm Sunday: Hosanna","r":"Matthew 21:8-9","x":"A massive crowd spread their cloaks on the road, while others cut branches from the trees and spread them on the road. The crowds that went ahead of Him and those that followed were shouting: “Hosanna to the Son of David!” “Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!” “Hosanna in the highest!”","teach":["Holy Week begins. Jesus rides into Jerusalem on a donkey, and the crowds spread their cloaks and branches on the road, shouting Hosanna, which means save us.","Many in that crowd expected a political king who would overthrow Rome. Within days, a crowd in the same city would shout crucify. Jesus knew, and He rode in anyway.","He came to save, just not the way they expected. Ask Him to be King of your life on His terms, not yours."],"pray":"Jesus, Hosanna: save me. Be my King, on Your terms. Keep me faithful when following You doesn't look like what I expected. Amen.","do":"Read Matthew 21:1-11 today and picture yourself in the crowd. What would you have shouted?"},{"d":41,"w":"Holy Week","t":"A house of prayer","r":"Mark 11:17","x":"Then Jesus began to teach them, and He declared, “Is it not written: ‘My house will be called a house of prayer for all the nations’? But you have made it ‘a den of robbers.’”","teach":["On Monday of Holy Week, Jesus walked into the temple and overturned the tables of the money changers. The place meant for prayer had become a marketplace.","His anger wasn't a temper tantrum. It was zeal for His Father's house, and for the outsiders who had been crowded out of the only court where they could pray.","If Jesus walked through your life this week, what tables would He overturn? What's crowding out prayer?"],"pray":"Jesus, clean out whatever in me crowds out prayer. Make my life a house of prayer again. Amen.","do":"Identify one thing that steals your prayer time and remove it for the rest of Holy Week."},{"d":42,"w":"Holy Week","t":"A kernel of wheat","r":"John 12:24","x":"Truly, truly, I tell you, unless a kernel of wheat falls to the ground and dies, it remains only a seed. But if it dies, it bears much fruit.","teach":["Days before the cross, Jesus explained what was coming with a picture from the farm. A seed that stays a seed stays alone. Only when it falls into the ground and dies does it bear much fruit.","His death would not be a defeat. It would be planting, and the harvest would be millions of lives.","The same pattern runs through our lives. Things we surrender to God, our pride, our plans, our control, become the soil for something new."],"pray":"Jesus, thank You for falling into the ground for me. Help me let go of what I need to surrender, trusting You to bring life from it. Amen.","do":"Name one thing you're holding too tightly, and pray over it every day this week: I let this go."},{"d":43,"w":"Holy Week","t":"By His wounds","r":"Isaiah 53:5","x":"But He was pierced for our transgressions, He was crushed for our iniquities; the punishment that brought us peace was upon Him, and by His stripes we are healed.","teach":["Seven hundred years before the cross, Isaiah described a servant who would suffer for others. Pierced for our transgressions. Crushed for our iniquities.","This is the heart of the gospel. The punishment that brought us peace fell on Him. Jesus didn't only die as an example. He died in our place.","Read this verse slowly and put your own name in it: He was pierced for my sins."],"pray":"Jesus, You were pierced for my sins and crushed for my iniquities. Thank You for taking what I deserved so that I could have peace. Amen.","do":"Read all of Isaiah 53 today, slowly, out loud if you can."},{"d":44,"w":"Holy Week","t":"Maundy Thursday: love one another","r":"John 13:34-35","x":"A new commandment I give you: Love one another. As I have loved you, so you also must love one another. By this everyone will know that you are My disciples, if you love one another.”","teach":["On the night before He died, Jesus washed His disciples' feet and gave them a new command: love one another as I have loved you.","The standard isn't how they love you, or how much they deserve it. It's how Jesus loved: on His knees, serving, even the one who would betray Him that night.","People will know you belong to Jesus by one thing: how you love. Look for a way to serve someone humbly today."],"pray":"Jesus, You knelt to wash feet. Teach me to love like that, humbly and practically, even when it costs me. Amen.","do":"Do a humble act of service for someone today, the kind of job nobody wants."},{"d":45,"w":"Holy Week","t":"Good Friday: it is finished","r":"John 19:30","x":"When Jesus had received the sour wine, He said, “It is finished.” And bowing His head, He yielded up His spirit.","teach":["On the cross, after hours of agony, Jesus said three words: “It is finished.” Then He gave up His spirit.","The word means completed, accomplished. Not partly done. Not done if you try hard enough. Finished. Everything needed to bring you back to God was done.","Today, don't rush past the cross toward Easter. Sit with what it cost, and let gratitude go deep."],"pray":"Jesus, You finished the work I could never do. Thank You for the cross. I rest in what You've done, not in what I do. Amen.","do":"Spend fifteen minutes in quiet today reading John 19, then simply say thank You."},{"d":46,"w":"Holy Week","t":"Holy Saturday: the waiting day","r":"Luke 23:55-56","x":"The women who had come with Jesus from Galilee followed, and they saw the tomb and how His body was placed. Then they returned to prepare spices and perfumes. And they rested on the Sabbath, according to the commandment.","teach":["The day after the crucifixion was silent. The women who loved Jesus prepared spices for His body and then rested on the Sabbath. They had no idea what Sunday would bring.","Holy Saturday is the day between: after the loss, before the answer. Many people live there for a long time, with grief, unanswered prayers, waiting.","If you're living in a Saturday right now, you're in good company, and Sunday is coming. If today feels unbearably dark, call or text 988 in the US."],"pray":"Lord, some parts of my life feel stuck between the cross and the empty tomb. Help me wait with hope. I trust that Sunday is coming. Amen.","do":"Pray for someone you know who is in a waiting season, and send them a message today."},{"d":47,"w":"Easter","t":"Easter: He is risen","r":"Matthew 28:5-6","x":"But the angel said to the women, “Do not be afraid, for I know that you are looking for Jesus, who was crucified. He is not here; He has risen, just as He said! Come, see the place where He lay.","teach":["He is risen. The women came to the tomb expecting to anoint a body. Instead, an angel told them: “He is not here; He has risen, just as He said!”","Everything changes because of this morning. Sin is paid for. Death is defeated. Every promise Jesus made is trustworthy, because He kept the biggest one.","Lent was the journey. Today is the celebration. Whatever you prayed, fasted and gave these 47 days, let it carry into a new life, one daily step at a time."],"pray":"Risen Jesus, You are alive! Thank You for defeating sin and death. Let resurrection life fill every part of me: my health, my money and my relationships. Amen.","do":"Tell someone today, in your own words, what Easter means to you."}]};try{window.dispatchEvent(new Event("flourish:seasons"))}catch(e){}